senses.gloss:
विंश, अस्, ई, अम्, twentieth; (अस्), m., scil. भाग,
a twentieth part (= विंशति-भाग, Manu VIII. 398);
(अस्), m., N. of a king.

विन्द, अस्, आ, अम्, finding, getting, gaining, one
who finds, &c.; (अस्), m., N. of a son of Jaya-sena;
of a son of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra.

वि-नाशन, अस्, ई, अम्, destroying, destructive,
ruinous; (अस्), m. one who destroys, a destroyer;
(अम्), n. destruction, annihilation.

वि-निर्धूत, अस्, आ, अम्, shaken off, driven away;
scattered in all directions, dissipated, dispersed; shaken
about, waved about.

विनिष्पिष् वि-निष्-पिष् (-निस्-पिष्), cl. 7. P.
-पिनष्टि, -पेष्टुम्, to grind to pieces, crush, bruise;
to rub together.

1. वि-नीय, ind. having taken away or removed;
having conducted; having guided or trained; having
inclined; having passed (as time &c.).

वि-नोदित, अस्, आ, अम्, driven away, dispelled,
dissipated, dispersed; dismissed; diverted, amused;
delighted, made happy; allayed, soothed.

विन्यस् वि-न्य्-अस् (वि-नि-), cl. 4. P. -अस्यति,
-असितुम्, to put or place down in different places;
to put down, deposit; to place in order, adjust, dis-
pose, arrange, distribute; to put or place on, lay on;
to set the mind on; to fix the eyes upon; to put or
place into; to deliver over.

वि-न्यस्यत्, अन्, अन्ती, अत्, putting down, putting
or placing on; setting or fixing the eyes upon;
arranging, fixing, settling, determining.
